Fix the MinGW compiler flags

-mno-ms-bitfields (https://musescore.org/node/22048, from the Qt 4 days)
changes the layout of structs with bit-fields away from the ABI that the
system Qt and all other MinGW libraries are built with, e.g. QSizePolicy.
Drop it, and define UNICODE/_UNICODE for clang-based MinGW toolchains too,
not only for GCC (CC_IS_MINGW is only set for GCC).

diff --git a/buildscripts/cmake/SetupBuildEnvironment.cmake b/buildscripts/cmake/SetupBuildEnvironment.cmake
index 019be14b..f4241149 100644
--- a/buildscripts/cmake/SetupBuildEnvironment.cmake
+++ b/buildscripts/cmake/SetupBuildEnvironment.cmake
@@ -83,10 +83,11 @@ if(CC_IS_MSVC)
     add_link_options("/NODEFAULTLIB:LIBCMT")
 endif()
 
-# MinGW-specific
-if(CC_IS_MINGW)
-    # https://musescore.org/node/22048
-    add_compile_options(-mno-ms-bitfields)
+# MinGW-specific (GCC and Clang)
+if(MINGW)
+    # No -mno-ms-bitfields (https://musescore.org/node/22048): it changes the
+    # layout of bit-field structs away from the ABI the system Qt and the
+    # other MinGW libraries are built with.
 
     if(NOT MUSE_COMPILE_BUILD_64)
         add_link_options("-Wl,--large-address-aware")
